  "notes": {
   "rerun": "After the verifier round (2026-11-02), three tests changed and were rerun with --reference (TESTS=amplitude0_matches_core,normals_match_finite_differences,object_size_carries_presets_over): their evidence above is from that rerun. The other 37 entries are from the family-sync run; those tests did not change.",
   "normals_match_finite_differences": "New case squeezed_chrome_type_amplitude_0_5 (V1). Green on 6a58487: its vertex shader used normalize() with no fallback, max 0.819 degrees, 0 normals over 5. The family-sync shader before the V1 fix kept the rest normal on 194 squeezed vertices: max 46.3 degrees.",
   "amplitude0_matches_core": "Two rows added at Object size 1.45 in both components (V2), plus after_fit_on_the_demo_torus (evidence only). Red by design: the 6a58487 material has no Objectsize, so it stays at the 6a58487 look.",
   "object_size_carries_presets_over": "Since the verifier round (V4) the test sets both Objectsize and the 6a58487 name Flowsize, so the 6a58487 material's motion scales too and the red measures only what C8 added: max 245/255, 15,861 to 21,713 px over 8/255 per case. The first record (only Objectsize set, so the old material's motion did not scale either) said 250/255 on 48,638 px.",
   "rerun_gap_round": "Verifier gap round (2026-11-02): the two new tests ran with --reference (TESTS=film_swirl_frequency_0_is_one_drifting_thickness,render_pass_keeps_foreground_in_front); their evidence above is from that run.",
   "film_swirl_frequency_0_is_one_drifting_thickness": "Red on 6a58487: there the shader used the constant 2.5 and ignored uFilm.w, so setting it to 0 still swirls (colour range 255 on the sheet). Delivered: one colour (range 0), (243, 254, 221) at 2 s and (189, 218, 16) at 30 s; Wobble speed 0: no change. The behaviour did not change in this round; the README's description of it did.",
   "render_pass_keeps_foreground_in_front": "Green on 6a58487: that material also wrote depth, so drawn into the scene render the ball stays in front (max 1/255). What changed in R2 is the route; the 6a58487 route is the test's Over TOP control, which paints the glass over the ball (max 246/255 on all 4,181 ball pixels over the glass). Mutation check (scratch copies, not shipped): the pixel shader writing gl_FragDepth = 0, or the vertex shader putting the glass at the near plane, makes the Render Pass route fail too (max 246/255)."
  }
 }
